#!RuleTest
#test CT-RUN-1 expect=violation domain=VS
#note CQ5 (a) + fold F1 — the define declares CT only for a root this SDTM run never consumes (define-xmlct): it does not put the define in play, so the Trial Summary supplies the CT. Define and TS ids are never mixed, and the ignored declaration is not flagged as a mismatch against the TS set (the note opens with the TS text, no "define declares" part).
#define-xml define-21-define-xmlct-only.xml
#ct-available sdtmct-2024-09-27
#expect-ct-mismatch "CT Packages is blank and no Define-XML declares CT for this run; CT taken from the Trial Summary: sdtmct-2024-09-27"
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset VS
col VSSTAT type=Char
---
BOGUS
---

dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVCDREF type=Char
col TSVCDVER type=Char
